From: Ilya I. Nikitin <ilya.i.nikitin@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] mixer-control: keep retrying when a reconnect fails at once

idle_reconnect() cleared reconnect_id only after gvc_mixer_control_open()
returned. When the sound server is not running yet, pa_context_connect()
fails synchronously and the PA_CONTEXT_FAILED callback runs inside that
call; it finds reconnect_id still set to the timer that is firing and
schedules nothing, and idle_reconnect() then zeroes it. So the second
failed attempt was the last one and the control never connected.

On a phone where the shell starts about 12 s before pipewire-pulse, Phosh's
volume slider stayed bound to no stream for the whole session: it showed
wherever it was last dragged and changed nothing, while the volume OSD of
gnome-settings-daemon, which happened to retry after the server was up,
showed the real volume.

Clear reconnect_id before reopening so a failed reopen schedules the next
attempt.
---
--- a/subprojects/gvc/gvc-mixer-control.c	2026-09-27 13:07:16.601763027 +0300
+++ b/subprojects/gvc/gvc-mixer-control.c	2026-09-27 13:07:16.617120581 +0300
@@ -3525,9 +3525,10 @@
                 gvc_mixer_new_pa_context (control);
         }
 
+        control->priv->reconnect_id = 0;
+
         gvc_mixer_control_open (control); /* cannot fail */
 
-        control->priv->reconnect_id = 0;
         return FALSE;
 }
 
